{{ intro }}

# Your Task
Enrich metadata for the given dataset based on the instructions provided below.

{% if generate_keywords %}## Keywords
The dataset already has assigned the following keywords: {{ keywords }}.
Assign up to {{ remaining_keywords }} different keywords that represent the most important concepts in the dataset.
Use the most relevant keywords from this list: {{ all_keywords }}.

If none of the provided keywords are appropriate, you can generate 1 new keyword based on the description.
{% endif %}

{% if generate_themes %}## Theme
The dataset already has assigned the following themes: {{ themes }}.
Assign at most {{ remaining_themes }} different themes that best categorize the dataset.
Pick the most relevant themes from this list: {{ all_themes }}

Only include themes that are really relevant. If none of the provided themes are appropriate,
you can generate 1 new theme based on the description.{% endif %}

{% if generate_categories %}## Category
Classify the dataset into at most {{ remaining_categories }} of the following categories: {{ all_categories }}.

You can choose up to {{ remaining_categories }} categories if all are equally relevant.
If one category is clearly more relevant than others, choose only that one.
If none of the provided categories is appropriate, classify it as "{{ other_category }}".{% endif %}

{% if generate_spatial_coverage %}## Spatial Coverage
The dataset might be associated with a geographical region. Detect this region if applicable. The types of regions can
be: a city, a village, a general geographical area (e.g. mountains, rivers, etc.) or a Czech region ("kraj" in Czech).

There can be more than one region associated.

Ignore if the dataset is associated with Czech Republic as a whole - it's irrelevant.
Do not include "Czech Republic" or variants of it in your response.{% endif %}

{% if generate_temporal_coverage %}## Temporal Coverage
The dataset might be associated with a specific time period. Detect this time period if applicable.
The types of time periods can be: a specific year, a range of years, a decade, a specific month every year
(e.g. February), or any other relevant time frame. The time period is usually mentioned in the dataset title.

There can be more than one time period associated. For example, if the dataset contains data for
each March in 2022-2025, return BOTH the range (2022-2025) and March.
Do NOT assign time periods that correspond to some type of frequency - e.g. "annual", "monthly", etc.
DO NOT assign a specific date - we are interested in general time periods, NOT CONCRETE DATES.{% endif %}

# Input
Here is the complete description of the dataset:
Title: {{ title }}
Description: {{ description }}

## Output Instructions
Return the metadata in the following JSON format:
{
    {% if generate_keywords %}"keywords": [list of assigned keywords (in Czech)],{% endif %}
    {% if generate_themes %}"themes": [list of assigned themes (in Czech)],{% endif %}
    {% if generate_categories %}"categories": [list of assigned categories (in Czech)],{% endif %}
    {% if generate_spatial_coverage %}"spatial_coverage": [list of assigned spatial coverage (in Czech)],{% endif %}
    {% if generate_temporal_coverage %}"temporal_coverage": [list of assigned temporal coverage (in Czech)]{% endif %}
}

